Q=[
make(1,"Which sentence uses capitalization correctly?",{"A":"My aunt lives in Taipei.","B":"my Aunt lives in taipei.","C":"My aunt lives in taipei.","D":"my aunt Lives in Taipei."},"A","The first word and proper place name Taipei need capital letters, while aunt does not.","Check the first word of the sentence and every proper noun, then leave common nouns lowercase.",["Locate the sentence beginning.","Check the first word My.","Identify Taipei as a proper place name.","Check that common noun aunt and verb lives remain lowercase.","Choose A because all capitalization rules are satisfied."],"easy"),
make(2,"Which sentence has the correct end punctuation for a question?",{"A":"Where is the science lab?","B":"Where is the science lab.","C":"Where is the science lab!","D":"Where is the science lab,"},"A","Where is the science lab? asks for information, so it ends with a question mark.","Identify the sentence function before selecting the punctuation mark.",["Read the sentence as a request for information.","Classify it as a question.","Match a question with a question mark.","Reject period, exclamation mark, and comma endings.","Choose A and read the punctuation aloud as a question."],"easy"),
make(3,"Which written time is clearest in a school notice?",{"A":"The meeting begins at 3:30 p.m.","B":"The meeting begins at 3.30 p.m?","C":"The meeting begins at 3:30pm,","D":"The meeting begins at p.m. 3:30."},"A","A uses a colon in the time, a space before p.m., and a period at the end of the statement.","Check the internal time separator, spacing, and sentence-ending punctuation in sequence.",["Find the time expression.","Check for a colon between hour and minute.","Check the space before p.m.","Check the final period for a statement.","Choose A because all format details are clear."],"medium"),
make(4,"Which date format is clearest in an English event notice?",{"A":"The fair is on October 12, 2026.","B":"The fair is on october 12 2026?","C":"The fair is on 12 October,.","D":"The fair is on October, 12 2026!"},"A","A capitalizes the month, separates the day and year with a comma, and ends the statement correctly.","Check month capitalization, date punctuation, and the final mark together.",["Identify the month name.","Capitalize October as a month.","Place a comma between day and year in this format.","Use a period for the notice statement.","Choose A because the date is readable and consistently formatted."],"medium"),
make(5,"Which opening is most appropriate for a short email to a teacher?",{"A":"Dear Ms. Chen,","B":"dear ms chen","C":"DEAR, Ms. Chen!","D":"Dear Ms Chen?"},"A","Dear Ms. Chen, uses capitalization, the title, the name, and a comma after the greeting.","Treat an email greeting as a formatted opening rather than an ordinary sentence or question.",["Identify the recipient as a teacher.","Capitalize Dear and the proper name.","Use Ms. before the surname.","Add a comma after the greeting.","Choose A because it follows a polite email format."],"easy"),
make(6,"Which version organizes three safety rules most clearly?",{"A":"1. Wear goggles. 2. Tie back long hair. 3. Wash your hands.","B":"1 Wear goggles 2 tie back hair 3 wash hands","C":"Safety: hair hands goggles maybe.","D":"Wear goggles, 3. wash hands, 1. hair."},"A","A uses numbered items, periods, and parallel imperative sentences, making the order easy to follow.","Check whether each rule has a number, punctuation, and the same clear command structure.",["Count the three separate rules.","Look for numbering that shows order.","Check each sentence for a period.","Check that every item is a complete command.","Choose A because the reader can scan and follow it."],"medium"),
make(7,"Which sentence uses quotation marks correctly for a speaker's exact words?",{"A":"Leo said, 'I finished the model.'","B":"Leo said, I finished the model.","C":"Leo said 'I finished the model'.","D":"Leo said; I finished the model?"},"A","A places the exact spoken words inside quotation marks and uses a comma before the quotation.","Identify reported exact speech and check the opening comma, quotation marks, and final period.",["Find the reporting phrase: Leo said.","Recognize the following words as exact speech.","Place the spoken sentence inside quotation marks.","Use a comma before the quotation and a period inside it.","Choose A because all dialogue punctuation is present."],"hard"),
make(8,"Which address line is formatted most clearly for a letter?",{"A":"25 Green Street, Kaohsiung","B":"25 green street kaohsiung?","C":"Green, 25 Street Kaohsiung!","D":"Kaohsiung 25, green street."},"A","A places the street number before the street name, capitalizes the proper names, and separates the city with a comma.","Read an address from specific location to broader location and apply proper-name capitalization.",["Identify the house number: 25.","Place it before the street name Green Street.","Capitalize the street and city names.","Separate the city with a comma.","Choose A because the address is ordered and readable."],"medium"),
make(9,"Which sentence is the clearest way to connect two related ideas in a report?",{"A":"The path was wet, so we walked slowly.","B":"The path was wet so, we walked slowly?","C":"The path was wet we walked slowly.","D":"The path, was wet; so we walked slowly!"},"A","A uses a comma before so to show that the wet path caused the slower walking, with a final period.","Identify the relationship between the clauses and choose punctuation that makes the connection visible.",["Identify the first complete idea: the path was wet.","Identify the result: we walked slowly.","Use so to connect cause and result.","Place a comma before so and a period at the end.","Choose A because the report is grammatical and easy to read."],"medium"),
make(10,"Which paragraph layout is best for a short report about a class garden?",{"A":"Begin with the purpose, give two supporting details, then end with the result in separate sentences.","B":"Put every idea in one very long sentence without punctuation.","C":"List the result first and omit what the class did.","D":"Use random spaces and capital letters to show new ideas."},"A","A gives a logical paragraph structure: purpose, evidence or details, and result, with readable sentence boundaries.","Evaluate organization by checking idea order, supporting information, conclusion, and sentence boundaries.",["Find the opening purpose of the report.","Add two details that support or explain it.","End with the result or conclusion.","Use separate sentences and consistent formatting.","Choose A because it organizes the reader's path through the report."],"hard"),
]
